review:
I thought these were quite bland for a Mexican dish, and that&#039;s after adding cumin, salt, garlic, white pepper...
After I try a new recipe, I always ask my husband (who is not picky at all) , &quot;Is this one a keeper? Should I make it again?&quot; He said, &quot;um, no. I liked all the cheese, but other than that, it was really bland.&quot;
If I had to tweak it, I would marinate the chicken in oil, lime juice and cumin. I would add some salt to the roux, mix some queso fresco into the roux, maybe use lightly fried corn tortillas in place of the flour ones so they don&#039;t get gummy. I don&#039;t know, just not a keeper.

Hi Inez;
WOW & more WOW!  This bread turned out just super-great.  I followed your recipe exactly, perfect amounts you specified.  I made 5 mini-loaves instead of using the 8 inch loaf pans.  The dough rose above the pans beautifully.  Baked them at 325 F for 35 minutes, browned perfect.  The texture of the bread was absolutely perfect.  I also rubbed the top of each loaf with some butter and this kept the crust from getting hard.  I ate 1/2 the mini-loaf soon as I could cut it.  I used butter and fresh liquid honey, Oh GEEZ, talk about wanting more, WOW!!!  The recipe is so easy to make and I just cannot see why anyone would have trouble getting the dough just right.  This is a must to bake every week.  Thanks so much Inez. 
\

Kelly, well you did it, these were a hit at the party!
I will admit however, they are time consuming to make, it would have been great if I'd had some extra hands around the house to do this with me.
Be sure the cherry tomatoes are not smooshy at all as that does make them difficult but all in all these were great and a good "conversation piece" as well :}
